  "tldr": "A randomized recurrent-event trial identifies separately capped baseline and residual marginals for a hypothetical switch while leaving their dependence unknown; the primitive recurrent-event paths themselves remain raw and unbounded. The substantive, prespecified restriction \\(B+W\\le H\\) turns that ambiguity into a Ferrers transport problem. The paper characterizes feasibility by exact Hall inequalities, derives atom-correct sharp threshold endpoints, proves that every feasible triple coupling has an observed-law-preserving raw-path FFRCISTG realization, identifies the complete shared-law threshold-value set, and computes exact minimax regret with an eligibility-greedy support oracle. On a relatively open cap-three family, the shared-law payoff set strictly tightens threshold-wise scalar bounds and reverses their minimax choice. A perspective confidence-polytope inversion covers the whole value set and every minimax threshold even at Hall and policy ties; efficient inference under general coarsening remains the first-class open question.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "The closest recurrent-event switching analysis supplies a no-carry-over condition and scalar sharp bounds one threshold at a time. It does not study a prespecified clinical capacity imposed on separately capped baseline and switched increments, characterize the resulting compatibility frontier, preserve one latent law across a threshold menu, certify extremal couplings by a raw-path FFRCISTG model, or cover the full robust-optimizer correspondence.",
    "niche": "A substantive cap on two separately capped summaries creates nested antidiagonal support without bounding the underlying recurrent-event paths, so Hall feasibility, discrete backward deficits, transport support functions, and finite response-tree gluing combine into an exact causal decision problem.",
    "fill": "The formal kernel joins an if-and-only-if Ferrers certificate and constructive raw-path causal lift to closed-form endpoints, a joint value polytope, exact shared-law regret, a strict open-family comparison with scalar-bound decisions, a nearly linear support oracle, and simultaneous confidence-set inversion."
  },
  "related_work": "JanvinRyalenSarvetStensrud2025 Assumption 1 supplies the no-carry-over template specialized here to separately capped post-landmark increments; its Proposition 1 and decision section supply threshold-wise scalar sharp bounds and regime logic. The new consequences arise only after combining that capped specialization with an independently prespecified capacity restriction: exact Hall feasibility, backward-deficit endpoints, one common-coupling payoff set, and a strict open-family regret separation. Strassen1965 gives the general support-constrained coupling principle, while Dahl2008 records staircase-support feasibility; their role here is methodological ancestry for the antidiagonal Hall reduction. ZhangRichardson2025 explains why weak and strict distribution events require separate care for discrete sums, which motivates the backward-deficit endpoint. HoffmanVeinott1993 informs the staircase greedy argument, so the algorithm is presented as a specialized computational component rather than a freestanding novelty claim. RichardsonRobins2013 provides the FFRCISTG semantics, and GreseleEtAl2022 frames the local-to-global causal-marginal obstruction addressed by the raw-path response-tree lift. MontielOleaQiuStoye2026 shows why joint payoff geometry matters for regret, whereas the present payoff set is generated by one capped transport law rather than a Gaussian reduced-form experiment. ChernozhukovHongTamer2007, AndrewsSoares2010, and Gafarov2025 inform the confidence inversion at binding inequalities and changing faces. BaerBuiMorkStrawdermanErtefaie2025 supplies the censoring-adjusted influence-function technology designated for the open semiparametric inference question.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The primitive counts are raw, nonnegative-integer-valued, and not bounded by \\(H\\). The capacity condition constrains the sum of a separately capped baseline count and a separately capped switched increment, so it is substantive rather than mechanically implied by the response-tree universe. Hall compatibility can reject a proposed cap statistically, but statistical compatibility cannot establish its clinical credibility. The response-tree theorem must explicitly audit every induced independence; a construction that assigns independent errors to all branches would strengthen FFRCISTG to an NPSEM model and would not establish the stated claim.",
  "honest_scope": "The finite-support identification for separately capped summaries, raw-path causal lift, common-law regret separation, rational witness, and confidence inversion are to be proved. Uniform semiparametric inference under coarsening at random is deliberately open. When the capacity restriction is removed and \\(\\mathcal M=\\{m\\}\\), the endpoint calculation must reduce to the discrete fixed-marginal sum bounds used by JanvinRyalenSarvetStensrud2025 and clarified by ZhangRichardson2025. SPRINT is only a conditional capped-loss consumer: a cap must be justified externally and prespecified at \\(k=300\\); the application is rejected if no credible cap exists or the censoring-adjusted Hall confidence system is infeasible.",
